4. Difference between Abstract class & interface?
  a. Abstract class can have default implementation , but interface can't.
  b. Abstract class does not support multiple inheritance, but interface does.
  c. we can define access modifiers in abstract class, but not in interface (by default everything is public)
  d. we can have fields in abstract class, but not in interface.
  e. Abstract class is performance wise faster than interface, as it does not need to search for implementation in derived class.
  f.Abstract class supports feature extension, but if we extent interface , then we have to define implementation in all derived classes.
  
